d the short of it</article-title><source>J Am Coll Cardiol</source><year>2002</year><volume>40</volume><fpage>424</fpage><lpage>427</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12142106</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><label>26</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kuntz</surname><given-names>RE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Importance of considering atherosclerosis progression when choosing a coronary revascularization strategy: the diabetespercutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty dilemma</article-title><source>Circulation</source><year>1999</year><volume>99</volume><fpage>847</fpage><lpage>851</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10027803</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><label>27</label><citation citation-type="confproc"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Serruys</surname><given-names>PW</given-names></name></person-group><source>ARTS-II of the sirolimus-eluting stent in the treatment of patients with multivessel de novo coronary artery lesions: late breaking clinical trial</source><conf-name>54th Annual Meeting</conf-name><conf-date>March 2005</conf-date><conf-loc>Orlando</conf-loc><comment>Presented at the American College of Cardiology</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B28"><label>28</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ben-Gal</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Moshkovitz</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Nesher</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Uretzky</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Braunstein</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Hendler</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Zivi</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Herz</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Mohr</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></pe